WEBVTT

01:59.536 --> 02:01.663
Sorry to keep you waiting, Captain.

02:03.373 --> 02:05.083
You want me to meet someone?

02:05.667 --> 02:08.586
Well, who is this person?

02:13.550 --> 02:16.094
A type you've never met before.

02:18.513 --> 02:19.347
Captain,

02:20.098 --> 02:21.975
they've all been like that.

02:22.517 --> 02:24.602
I'm used to new types.

02:24.686 --> 02:26.104
Here's a question for you.

02:26.813 --> 02:29.357
What is the most powerful animal
in history?

02:30.817 --> 02:32.193
Is this a serious question?

02:33.027 --> 02:35.155
Clearly, you don't mean Yujiro Hanma.

02:35.697 --> 02:38.867
Siberian tigers? Lions?
What's this about anyway?

02:39.450 --> 02:42.996
Not the most powerful on Earth.
The most powerful in history.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.874
Huh? What kind of game is this?

02:45.957 --> 02:47.208
Answer the question.

02:47.292 --> 02:49.752
You mean like dinosaurs? Mammoths?

02:50.336 --> 02:51.671
It's a dinosaur.

02:51.754 --> 02:53.756
What's the most powerful dinosaur?

02:54.799 --> 02:56.009
Captain...

02:56.092 --> 02:57.760
Just answer the question.

02:58.511 --> 02:59.888
A T-Rex?

03:00.388 --> 03:02.765
I think it's called "Tyrannosaurus."

03:07.145 --> 03:09.272
You know I can't read English.

03:15.695 --> 03:16.529
Who's this?

03:16.613 --> 03:19.657
A man stronger than a T-Rex.

03:19.741 --> 03:22.368
In fact, I'd call him a "male."

03:28.750 --> 03:31.753
That's... that's a dinosaur, isn't it?

03:31.836 --> 03:33.171
Isn't it a T-Rex?

03:33.755 --> 03:35.840
The dynamite must have exposed it.

03:35.924 --> 03:37.717
Salt rock is a good preserver,

03:37.800 --> 03:40.678
but it's been preserved
in unbelievably excellent condition.

03:40.762 --> 03:42.805
And that's a human.

03:42.889 --> 03:45.391
Yeah, there's no doubt about that.

03:45.475 --> 03:47.268
But how can this be explained?

03:47.852 --> 03:49.103
Does it even matter?

03:49.646 --> 03:51.231
It's just like it looks.

03:51.314 --> 03:54.275
Were humans even around in that era?

03:54.776 --> 03:56.236
Does that even matter?

03:56.319 --> 03:58.196
Clearly, this human lived then.

03:58.279 --> 04:00.448
It looks like he's attacking the T-Rex.

04:01.324 --> 04:02.200
But

04:02.784 --> 04:05.703
considering its size,
that's just not possible.

04:06.287 --> 04:09.582
It's likely this is his intense reaction
to being attacked.

04:10.124 --> 04:13.795
Even if that's true,
he's got a heck of a lot of guts.

04:14.295 --> 04:15.880
What do we do now?

04:15.964 --> 04:17.590
This is an incredible find.

04:18.424 --> 04:20.051
First, we'll contact HQ.

04:27.308 --> 04:31.020
I truly appreciate
your unearthing of this incredible find.

04:31.104 --> 04:34.232
To be honest, it's making me tremble.

04:34.315 --> 04:35.858
Thank you, sir.

04:35.942 --> 04:39.362
We're not exactly sure
what to think of this discovery either.

04:39.445 --> 04:41.072
I agree.

04:41.155 --> 04:45.118
We've always believed humans
first appeared seven million years ago.

04:45.201 --> 04:48.621
Who'd have thought it would be
pushed back to the Jurassic period.

04:49.205 --> 04:52.625
It goes without saying,
but this cannot be made public.

04:53.209 --> 04:57.714
This would run roughshod
over present-day theories.

04:57.797 --> 05:00.174
The impact it would have is too great.

05:00.258 --> 05:03.761
Information about this
must only gradually be made public.

05:03.845 --> 05:05.763
We're gonna revive him, right?

05:05.847 --> 05:08.182
Don't be ridiculous, Allen!

05:08.891 --> 05:12.729
This isn't like giving mouth-to-mouth
by a pool.

05:12.812 --> 05:16.524
Uh, is that sort of thing even possible?

05:16.607 --> 05:18.276
In the year 2000,

05:19.402 --> 05:23.990
<i>while in New Mexico,
Professor Russel Breland discovered</i>

05:24.073 --> 05:29.245
<i>tiny drops of water in a piece
of salt rock from 250 million years ago.</i>

05:29.954 --> 05:32.206
<i>After very carefully extracting them,</i>

05:32.290 --> 05:35.251
<i>he found that they were seawater
from 250 million years ago.</i>

05:35.877 --> 05:36.919
<i>What's more,</i>

05:37.003 --> 05:40.840
<i>microorganisms from back then
had been perfectly preserved.</i>

05:41.341 --> 05:43.384
<i>He placed them in the ideal environment,</i>

05:43.468 --> 05:47.305
<i>administering the perfect nutrition,
stimulation and temperature.</i>

05:47.805 --> 05:50.183
<i>Then, 120 days later,</i>

05:50.725 --> 05:54.771
<i>every last one of them was revived.</i>

05:55.480 --> 05:57.648
You mean they hadn't died?

05:57.732 --> 06:00.526
Of course,
they couldn't be described as alive.

06:01.069 --> 06:03.404
But they hadn't died either.

06:03.988 --> 06:08.701
They had been waiting
for the ideal conditions,

06:08.785 --> 06:10.787
for 250 million years.

06:12.205 --> 06:13.164
It was the salt.

06:13.831 --> 06:18.586
<i>The strong salt
in the 1,000-meter-thick salt rock layer</i>

06:18.669 --> 06:22.757
<i>protected the microorganisms
from the inescapable force of time.</i>

06:23.758 --> 06:26.094
Meaning it's theoretically possible

06:26.177 --> 06:28.346
to bring Pickle here back to life.

06:28.429 --> 06:29.680
Allen!

06:29.764 --> 06:32.850
Reviving life is the realm of God.

06:32.934 --> 06:34.560
Treat it with more respect.

06:34.644 --> 06:37.063
Those were amoebas. This is a human.

06:37.146 --> 06:40.942
They're basically as different
as a bicycle and a space shuttle.

06:41.025 --> 06:43.653
That is an appropriate comparison.

06:44.195 --> 06:46.864
But how will you make up
the difference between them?

06:46.948 --> 06:49.826
Naturally, with this and this.

06:51.285 --> 06:56.499
<i>Otherwise, a space shuttle and a bicycle
are both just kinds of vehicles.</i>

07:00.294 --> 07:02.213
<i>Today is Day 91</i>

07:02.922 --> 07:05.967
<i>of Professor Payne's
Pickle revival project.</i>

07:06.717 --> 07:10.221
<i>A massive number of pulse electrodes
have been attached to Pickle.</i>

07:10.805 --> 07:13.599
<i>And since Pickle lived
during the Jurassic period,</i>

07:13.683 --> 07:17.186
<i>the temperature in the lab
has been adjusted accordingly.</i>

07:17.687 --> 07:18.604
It's hot.

07:19.313 --> 07:23.151
<i>Pickle is immersed in a solution
that closely resembles his bodily fluids.</i>

07:23.234 --> 07:26.529
<i>And this device perfectly mimics
the cycle of the tides</i>

07:27.238 --> 07:30.199
<i>and the tempo
that is the mother of all life.</i>

07:30.700 --> 07:34.370
<i>But none of this has awakened Pickle.</i>

07:37.874 --> 07:39.625
<i>The test is a failure.</i>

07:45.423 --> 07:46.257
<i>Yuck.</i>

07:47.091 --> 07:48.634
<i>I'd sure love some steak.</i>

07:52.472 --> 07:54.140
<i>I'll be the first human...</i>

07:54.223 --> 07:56.142
<i>in fact, the first being in history...</i>

08:03.024 --> 08:07.320
<i>I'll be the first male to eat a T-Rex!</i>

08:10.907 --> 08:11.741
<i>Impossible...</i>

08:12.492 --> 08:15.536
<i>The muscle tissue of the T-Rex</i>

08:15.620 --> 08:19.540
<i>and the tissue found in his stomach match.</i>

08:20.124 --> 08:22.793
<i>There's only one thing this can mean.</i>

08:23.503 --> 08:26.797
<i>Pickle preyed on the T-Rex!</i>

08:28.382 --> 08:32.053
<i>The thing weighs over ten tons,
so just this little bit...</i>

08:32.762 --> 08:35.848
<i>Two hundred grams won't be missed.</i>

08:51.948 --> 08:54.325
<i>A Tyrannosaurus steak!</i>

08:58.079 --> 08:59.956
<i>Hmm... Is this like beef?</i>

09:00.039 --> 09:01.707
<i>No, maybe lamb?</i>

09:01.791 --> 09:04.585
<i>Or maybe like the whale I had in Japan?</i>

09:05.419 --> 09:10.091
<i>Anyway, it is a little stringy,
but it's actually pretty good.</i>

09:14.178 --> 09:17.515
<i>After awakening from his long sleep
of 200 million years,</i>

09:18.140 --> 09:19.809
<i>the man sat stunned.</i>

09:21.227 --> 09:23.980
<i>What he saw was
a profoundly mysterious sight.</i>

09:24.689 --> 09:26.440
<i>Straight lines running vertically.</i>

09:27.149 --> 09:29.360
<i>A wall covered in bright lights.</i>

09:30.319 --> 09:32.238
<i>Circles. Transparent objects.</i>

09:33.030 --> 09:34.991
<i>Everything he laid eyes on</i>

09:35.074 --> 09:39.078
<i>was something that hadn't existed
a short time ago to him.</i>

09:53.926 --> 09:55.595
<i>Surrounded in mystery,</i>

09:56.095 --> 09:59.015
<i>there was only one thing he recognized.</i>

10:00.141 --> 10:01.350
<i>A smell.</i>

10:01.434 --> 10:03.436
<i>Yes, this was something he knew.</i>

10:04.228 --> 10:07.648
<i>And it was coming from down that path.</i>

10:17.241 --> 10:18.075
Huh?

10:21.037 --> 10:23.039
<i>In an emergency, humans don't think.</i>

10:23.623 --> 10:28.252
<i>A massive number of thoughts occur
all at once in no specific order.</i>

10:29.253 --> 10:30.087
<i>Pickle!</i>

10:30.171 --> 10:31.005
<i>He's giant!</i>

10:31.088 --> 10:33.382
<i>He woke up?!
But he didn't after all we did!</i>

10:33.466 --> 10:35.301
<i>He knows I stole part of the T-Rex!</i>

10:35.384 --> 10:36.677
<i>What a beast!</i>

10:36.761 --> 10:39.889
<i>My only weapon is a box cutter.
Impossible! I'll never win!</i>

10:39.972 --> 10:42.183
<i>I'll die instantly,
no matter what my weapon is!</i>

10:42.266 --> 10:44.602
<i>But there is a gun in the drawer.</i>

10:44.685 --> 10:45.853
<i>Could I win with a gun?</i>

10:45.936 --> 10:47.146
<i>I don't think I could!</i>

10:47.647 --> 10:48.856
<i>Impossible! It's obvious!</i>

10:48.939 --> 10:50.316
<i>He'll punch me in an instant!</i>

10:50.399 --> 10:51.942
<i>He doesn't know what a gun is!</i>

10:52.026 --> 10:53.903
<i>Of course he does. He's a savage!</i>

10:55.279 --> 10:58.949
<i>No way! He's putting the whole
150 grams in his mouth at once?!</i>

10:59.033 --> 11:00.743
<i>What's more, he didn't even chew.</i>

11:02.161 --> 11:03.579
<i>He's looking! With hostility?</i>

11:03.663 --> 11:05.206
<i>Wait. What? What's he doing?</i>

11:07.333 --> 11:09.293
<i>Does he think I'm food?</i>

11:09.377 --> 11:11.045
<i>He doesn't think I'm his enemy!</i>

11:11.128 --> 11:13.798
<i>Or maybe I'm not suitable to be food.</i>

11:13.881 --> 11:15.841
<i>He knows I'd taste disgusting.</i>

11:15.925 --> 11:17.093
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

11:17.176 --> 11:18.469
<i>But also kinda humiliating.</i>

11:20.930 --> 11:22.723
<i>But just in case...</i>

11:23.516 --> 11:24.350
<i>Just in case.</i>

11:25.059 --> 11:27.103
<i>As the representative of civilized humans,</i>

11:27.687 --> 11:30.856
<i>I'll make one thing clear to this guy.</i>

11:31.899 --> 11:34.360
<i>Wait a sec. What's this guy doing anyway?</i>

11:34.443 --> 11:35.861
<i>Is he looking for something?</i>

11:39.198 --> 11:41.158
<i>Wait. Why's he looking at me like that?</i>

11:42.201 --> 11:45.121
<i>What?! He's mad. He growled?</i>

11:48.874 --> 11:50.418
Wait! Just a moment!

11:50.501 --> 11:52.670
What is it? Tell me. Tell me!

11:52.753 --> 11:54.255
What do you want? What is it?

11:55.464 --> 11:57.883
Stop! Hold it right there!

11:57.967 --> 12:00.177
Stop! Pickle, stop!

12:00.261 --> 12:02.763
This is a handgun! Okay? You know?

12:02.847 --> 12:04.974
<i>There's no way he understands!</i>

12:05.057 --> 12:06.809
<i>Should I shoot? Where though?</i>

12:07.351 --> 12:08.269
<i>At his feet!</i>

12:08.352 --> 12:09.645
<i>That'll scare him!</i>

12:15.067 --> 12:16.318
<i>What?!</i>

12:24.994 --> 12:27.079
<i>The gun, a product of civilization,</i>

12:27.705 --> 12:30.332
<i>was fired three times into his bare flesh.</i>

12:30.416 --> 12:33.085
It... it's your own fault!

12:33.961 --> 12:37.131
<i>The 9mm bullets
were not up to the task of piercing</i>

12:37.757 --> 12:40.509
<i>the abdominal muscles
of the Jurassic fighter, Pickle.</i>

12:41.427 --> 12:43.345
<i>For Allen, who was still in shock,</i>

12:43.929 --> 12:46.599
<i>this was the night's greatest shock.</i>

13:01.697 --> 13:03.824
<i>This is insane!</i>

13:03.908 --> 13:05.242
<i>Why am I alone?</i>

13:05.326 --> 13:07.995
<i>Why am I alone at night in a lab?!</i>

13:08.078 --> 13:09.747
<i>It's a sci-fi horror flick!</i>

13:13.167 --> 13:15.669
<i>It's over. My life ends here.</i>

13:27.306 --> 13:28.891
<i>Wait, is he</i>

13:29.975 --> 13:31.227
<i>demanding something?</i>

13:32.019 --> 13:34.146
<i>That's it. He's making a demand.</i>

13:35.022 --> 13:36.148
<i>He wants something.</i>

13:36.232 --> 13:37.858
<i>He wants me to do something.</i>

13:38.859 --> 13:41.278
<i>In any case, he's not going to kill--</i>

13:51.497 --> 13:52.790
<i>I forgot</i>

13:54.333 --> 13:55.292
<i>that he's</i>

13:55.876 --> 13:58.045
<i>like a savage beast.</i>

14:00.381 --> 14:03.551
<i>That I could be killed,
even if he's just playing.</i>

14:04.134 --> 14:07.179
<i>At any rate, I've got to get there.</i>

14:08.848 --> 14:10.432
<i>I'll escape into here.</i>

14:11.392 --> 14:14.311
<i>Hurry. I've got to hurry.</i>

14:17.898 --> 14:19.817
<i>I'm too late.</i>

14:29.785 --> 14:31.328
<i>What?!</i>

14:40.462 --> 14:41.338
<i>Wait a second.</i>

14:42.756 --> 14:45.801
<i>Did I just trap him?</i>

14:48.304 --> 14:50.723
You confined him?

14:51.348 --> 14:53.809
I can understand why you're surprised.

14:53.893 --> 14:55.644
But it's all true.

14:56.562 --> 14:58.647
The fact that Pickle was revived

14:58.731 --> 15:01.859
and that he was
ultimately imprisoned in the freezer.

15:02.484 --> 15:07.281
And it must have been you who called
this ridiculous crowd.

15:07.364 --> 15:09.491
Yes, that was my decision.

15:09.575 --> 15:11.744
What did you expect them to do?

15:11.827 --> 15:14.163
You'll understand once you see him.

15:14.246 --> 15:15.706
What will I understand?

15:15.789 --> 15:19.376
Those five police cars
are definitely not an overreaction.

15:19.960 --> 15:21.420
Such a fool.

15:21.503 --> 15:22.671
With all due respect,

15:23.255 --> 15:25.591
when it comes to knowledge of Pickle,

15:25.674 --> 15:28.135
I now know more than you do, Professor.

15:28.719 --> 15:31.513
Bullets bounce off of his body.

15:32.389 --> 15:36.101
Besides that, he threw the bullets back
and pierced my shoulder.

15:36.602 --> 15:39.396
Even a major-league pitcher
couldn't do that!

15:40.189 --> 15:42.650
I can't even be sure
five police cars is enough.

15:42.733 --> 15:45.653
That doesn't really matter now.

15:45.736 --> 15:46.779
Huh?

15:47.404 --> 15:48.447
Sorry.

15:48.530 --> 15:52.326
We've checked the building's floor plans
and located the freezer.

15:53.202 --> 15:54.870
We're going to storm it now,

15:54.954 --> 15:58.123
but it's possible we may
have to give up on capturing him alive.

15:58.207 --> 16:00.584
What? Wait, you can't mean that.

16:00.668 --> 16:02.419
You'll never succeed.

16:02.503 --> 16:03.337
Who are you?

16:03.420 --> 16:04.797
I'm Albert Payne.

16:05.756 --> 16:07.883
Of all places,

16:08.384 --> 16:11.553
I never imagined
I would meet a Nobel laureate here.

16:12.221 --> 16:15.307
- I am--
- Save the introductions for later.

16:15.391 --> 16:17.643
I say this for your own good.

16:17.726 --> 16:20.813
Request that the army
be brought in immediately.

16:22.439 --> 16:25.359
I don't mean to defy a Nobel laureate,

16:25.901 --> 16:28.779
but I was told
there is only one perpetrator.

16:28.862 --> 16:31.949
He may have the strength
and stamina of a wild beast,

16:32.700 --> 16:35.327
but that is all he is.

16:35.911 --> 16:38.956
When did this beast turn into King Kong?

16:39.456 --> 16:43.085
I thought about how
I should describe the man.

16:43.168 --> 16:44.837
But King Kong

16:45.379 --> 16:48.340
is certainly an appropriate comparison.

17:02.438 --> 17:04.440
Contact HQ.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.026
Request backup. Twenty men...

17:07.568 --> 17:08.610
No, 30!

17:19.621 --> 17:21.665
Contact the army immediately!

17:21.749 --> 17:23.208
It's an emergency!

17:23.292 --> 17:24.543
It's enraged.

17:25.586 --> 17:26.920
His reason for living,

17:27.463 --> 17:28.756
his food,

17:29.339 --> 17:31.341
and his pride...

17:31.925 --> 17:34.344
He has become enraged that his rival

17:34.428 --> 17:35.846
has been stolen from him.

17:40.893 --> 17:44.480
<i>The police informed the army
that an armed terrorist had entered</i>

17:45.355 --> 17:48.108
<i>the nuclear waste isolation plant.</i>

17:49.318 --> 17:52.196
<i>The army was actually
quite happy to be deployed.</i>

17:52.946 --> 17:53.822
<i>That's because</i>

17:55.074 --> 17:58.452
<i>it was the perfect opportunity to test out</i>

17:58.535 --> 18:01.497
<i>a new weapon
that was still under development.</i>

18:02.581 --> 18:06.502
Your false report
of an armed terrorist in a nuclear site

18:06.585 --> 18:08.087
is unforgivable.

18:08.712 --> 18:11.590
But now that I see the situation,

18:12.174 --> 18:16.512
he definitely has the destructive power
of a suicide bomber.

18:17.096 --> 18:19.765
But even if he is on par with King Kong,

18:19.848 --> 18:21.141
he's unarmed.

18:21.725 --> 18:23.644
Why don't you just shoot and kill him?

18:23.727 --> 18:25.979
You're exactly right,

18:26.063 --> 18:28.899
but there isn't time now to explain.

18:28.982 --> 18:31.110
There's only one thing that's certain.

18:31.693 --> 18:35.906
That man is a treasure
to the entire human race.

18:36.990 --> 18:40.119
That naked barbarian is,
in a certain respect,

18:40.202 --> 18:44.289
more valuable
than the president of any country.

18:44.373 --> 18:48.043
You, too, are a treasure
of the human race.

18:48.877 --> 18:52.339
Since you are a Nobel laureate,
I will accept your request.

18:53.132 --> 18:55.551
We will capture him without harming him!

18:56.802 --> 18:59.680
The Multi-Purpose Battle Machine, MPBM,

18:59.763 --> 19:03.433
will be officially deployed next year.

19:04.101 --> 19:07.521
<i>To reach this point, the operator
spent the last two and a half years</i>

19:07.604 --> 19:09.940
<i>using it for everything in his daily life.</i>

19:10.649 --> 19:13.819
<i>Thanks to that, he can use it
to do absolutely anything.</i>

19:14.695 --> 19:17.406
<i>He could lead several lions
around by the nose,</i>

19:17.489 --> 19:19.074
<i>destroy military vehicles,</i>

19:19.658 --> 19:21.577
<i>or even knit with it.</i>

19:27.166 --> 19:31.295
But why doesn't he leave that place?

19:31.378 --> 19:33.130
He's defending something.

19:33.714 --> 19:34.840
Defending what?

19:34.923 --> 19:36.216
Most likely...

19:36.300 --> 19:37.426
"Most likely"?

19:37.968 --> 19:39.011
Probably...

19:39.094 --> 19:40.179
"Probably"?

19:40.262 --> 19:41.096
His era.

19:41.930 --> 19:43.098
"Era"?

19:43.182 --> 19:45.100
What era, Professor Payne?

19:45.684 --> 19:46.518
You see...

19:47.186 --> 19:48.687
What era, Professor?

19:49.188 --> 19:51.815
He's defending his era...

19:51.899 --> 19:53.483
"His era"?

19:55.569 --> 19:57.237
From our era.

20:06.914 --> 20:09.082
<i>He smashed the armor plate with a punch!</i>

20:09.166 --> 20:10.334
<i>You gotta be kiddin' me!</i>

20:10.417 --> 20:11.460
<i>His neck!</i>

20:11.543 --> 20:13.337
<i>The hell with capturing him alive!</i>

20:13.420 --> 20:14.796
<i>He's gonna kill me!</i>

20:15.297 --> 20:16.340
<i>His neck!</i>

20:19.176 --> 20:20.427
<i>What?</i>

20:44.576 --> 20:46.203
<i>Is this even possible?</i>

20:46.870 --> 20:49.414
<i>The thing taking on
the armed forces of the world,</i>

20:49.498 --> 20:53.210
<i>in fact, the most powerful army of all,
the US Armed Forces,</i>

20:53.835 --> 20:56.463
<i>is a single beast?</i>

20:57.047 --> 20:59.091
<i>A single living being is taking them on?</i>

21:00.300 --> 21:02.052
<i>We're using the latest tanks.</i>

21:03.053 --> 21:04.721
<i>We're using military helicopters.</i>

21:05.430 --> 21:07.474
<i>We're using armed troops.</i>

21:08.100 --> 21:09.476
<i>Is that acceptable?</i>

21:09.559 --> 21:11.979
Captain, it's in sight now.

21:12.062 --> 21:13.689
<i>Of course it's not.</i>

21:14.773 --> 21:15.607
Stop.

21:23.198 --> 21:24.616
I'll be back in a minute.

21:25.200 --> 21:26.702
What? Captain!

21:27.536 --> 21:32.124
<i>The soldier felt ashamed
as he walked among the grisly sight.</i>

21:33.709 --> 21:38.130
<i>He saw that modern weapons were frail
in the face of a powerful person.</i>

21:39.006 --> 21:41.008
<i>As a soldier well versed in weaponry...</i>

21:41.591 --> 21:43.760
<i>As a man,</i>

21:44.344 --> 21:45.679
<i>and as a male,</i>

21:46.221 --> 21:48.682
<i>a feeling beyond respect grew within him.</i>

21:53.228 --> 21:57.149
<i>For the first time
since Pickle had awakened,</i>

21:57.232 --> 21:59.651
<i>he saw eyes that held no enmity.</i>

22:00.319 --> 22:02.154
I want to know more about you.

22:02.821 --> 22:04.656
<i>Naturally, he didn't understand words.</i>

22:05.240 --> 22:07.909
<i>Even so, there was communication.</i>

22:08.744 --> 22:09.661
Let's go

22:09.745 --> 22:13.415
to where there are others like you.

22:16.585 --> 22:17.544
To Japan.

22:18.378 --> 22:21.048
<i>Pickle is headed for Japan.</i>
